.TH DIPIRADIOHEAD 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipiradiohead \- re-mux an Icecast/Shoutcast stream as a DVB-IPI multicast
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipiradiohead
.B \-i
.I uri
[\fB\-\-sid\fP \fIn\fP] [\fB\-\-sdt\fP \fIname\fP] [\fB\-i\fP \fIuri\fP ...]
{\fB\-m\fP \fIgroup\fP:\fIport\fP | \fB\-R\fP \fIuri\fP} [\fIoptions\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipiradiohead
fetches one or more Icecast/Shoutcast streams over
.B http://
or
.B https://
and re-muxes them, without transcoding, as one DVB-IPI multicast (or one or
more RIST links). A single
.B \-i
produces a normal SPTS; more than one
.B \-i
produces an MPTS, one program per input. Icecast/Shoutcast as an input
source is not itself part of DVB; it exists here to bridge real-world
streaming sources into a DVB-IPI output.
.PP
Output is UDP or RTP multicast via
.BR \-m ,
one or more RIST peers via
.B \-R
(bonded onto a single sender, requires librist), or both at once; at least
one of the two is required.
.B dipiradiohead
generates PAT/PMT/SDT/NIT/EIT signaling itself, including now-playing EIT
present-event text taken from ICY
.B StreamTitle
metadata or inline ID3v2
.B TIT2
/
.B TPE1
tags, auto-detected per stream; this ICY/ID3-to-EIT mapping is a
.B dipiradiohead
addition, not a DVB-IPI feature.
.PP
.B https://
sources are TLS-verified by default (certificate chain, hostname, expiry);
.B \-k
disables all three for self-signed lab or test sources. HTTPS support needs
OpenSSL (libssl) and is a build-time option; a build without it fails
cleanly on any
.B https://
source rather than connecting insecurely.
.PP
.B dipiradiohead
can also scramble its output. As a DVB Simulcrypt SCS and EMMG-side MUX
(ETSI TS 103 197, protocol versions 2 and 3) it drives one or more ECMGs via
.B \-\-cas\-algo
/
.BR \-\-cas\-ecmg ,
scrambling with CISSA (ETSI TS 103 127, needs OpenSSL) or CSA1/CSA2 (need
libdvbcsa, loaded at runtime if present). Independently of Simulcrypt, it
also supports standalone BISS scrambling with no ECMG/EMMG at all: legacy
BISS1 Mode 1, BISS2 Mode 1/E, and BISS2 Mode CA (EBU Tech 3292/3292-s1,
per-receiver RSA-2048-OAEP entitlement). Simulcrypt CAS and the BISS modes
are mutually exclusive with each other.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIuri\fR
Icecast/Shoutcast source,
.B http://
or
.BR https:// .
Repeatable; each
.B \-i
becomes one program of the output MPTS (or the single program of an SPTS
if given only once).
.TP
.B \-\-sid \fIn\fR
service_id / program_number for the
.B \-i
immediately before this option. Default: auto-assigned, lowest unused
number.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sdt " " \fIname\fR
SDT service_name for the
.B \-i
immediately before this option. Default: auto (
.B dipiradiohead
for a single input, "dipiradiohead \fIn\fR" per input for an MPTS).
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " " \fIgroup\fR:\fIport\fR
Output multicast group:port. Use
.RI [ addr6 ]: port
for IPv6. Required unless
.B \-R
is given.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Outgoing multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rtp
Wrap output in RTP. Default is plain UDP. Applies only to the
.B \-m
output.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-ttl " " \fIn\fR
Multicast TTL / hop limit. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-rist " " \fIuri\fR
.B rist://host:port[?query]
output. Repeatable; every peer bonds onto a single RIST sender (requires
librist). May be combined with
.BR \-m .
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIp\fR
RIST profile,
.B simple
or
.BR main .
Applies only to
.B \-R
peers. Default:
.BR simple .
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fIpsk\fR
RIST pre-shared key. Applies only to
.B \-R
peers. Requires
.BR \-\-profile\ main .
.TP
.B \-\-cname \fIname\fR
RIST cname. Applies only to
.B \-R
peers. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer \fIms\fR
RIST recovery buffer, in milliseconds. Applies only to
.B \-R
peers. Default: library default.
.SS "Stream Identifiers"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nit " " \fItext\fR
NIT network_name.
.TP
.B \-\-tsid \fIn\fR
transport_stream_id. Default: 1.
.TP
.B \-\-onid \fIn\fR
original_network_id. Default: 1.
.SS "Reliability and TLS"
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-error " " \fIseconds\fR
On input error, reconnect after N seconds. Default: fail once. Always
retries, regardless of this option, when more than one
.B \-i
is given.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Skip TLS verification on
.B https://
sources: self-signed certificates, hostname mismatch, and expiry are all
ignored.
.SS "Logging and Metrics"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print periodic statistics on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
Colorize log output:
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket path for metrics output. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id for metrics. Metrics are disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Metrics snapshot interval, in seconds. Default:
.BR 5 .
.SS "CAS Scrambling: Simulcrypt"
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-algo \fIa\fR
Enable CAS scrambling:
.BR cissa ,
.BR csa2 ,
or
.BR csa1 .
Default: disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg \fIep\fR
ECMG address,
.BR tcp://host:port .
Repeatable, one CAS vendor per
.BR \-\-cas\-ecmg .
At least one is required with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: ECMG protocol version,
.B 2
or
.BR 3 .
Default: auto-negotiate.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-super\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: Super_CAS_id, decimal or 0x-hex. Required
per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: ECM_id. Required per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: output PID for its ECM stream. Default:
.BR 0x0020 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-port \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: our EMMG listener port. Default:
.BR 8002 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: EMMG protocol version,
.B 2
or
.BR 3 .
Default: accept whichever the EMMG client proposes.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: output PID for its EMM stream. Default:
.BR 0x0021 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-resilience \fIr\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: behavior on that vendor's own ECMG loss,
.BR frozen ,
.BR cycling ,
or
.BR silent .
Default:
.BR frozen .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-required
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
immediately before this option: that vendor's outage forces the global
fallback (see
.BR \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear )
regardless of other vendors' state.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cp\-duration \fIms\fR
Crypto-period duration in milliseconds, shared by every configured vendor.
Default:
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear
On total CAS outage (or a
.B \-\-cas\-required
vendor going down): switch content to clear-to-air instead of staying
scrambled on the last known-good control word.
.SS "CAS Scrambling: BISS"
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-sw \fIhex32\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode 1/E: a static 32 hex character Session Word, scrambling
with CISSA. No ECMG/EMMG. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-emit\-esw \fIid\fR
With
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw :
log the AES-128-ECB Encrypted Session Word for the given 32 hex character
receiver ID, for out-of-band distribution to that receiver.
.TP
.B \-\-biss1\-sw \fIhex12\fR
Enable legacy BISS1 Mode 1: a static 12 hex character Session Word,
scrambling with CSA1. Mutually exclusive with
.B \-\-biss2\-sw
and
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers \fIdir\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode CA: a directory of PEM public keys, one per entitled
receiver or group. Rescanned on
.BR SIGHUP ;
removing a receiver from the directory revokes it and forces a Session Key
change. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-biss1\-sw ,
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw ,
and
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-session\-id \fIn\fR
Administratively unique entitlement_session_id, decimal or 0x-hex, 16 bit.
Default: random at startup.
.SS "Process Control"
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipiradiohead \-i https://example.com/radio.m3u \-\-sdt \(dqChannel 1\(dq \-m 239.1.1.1:5000
Single station, plain UDP multicast output.
.TP
.B dipiradiohead \-i http://example.com/somechannel/aac \-\-sdt \(dqSome Channel\(dq \-i https://example.com/radio.m3u \-\-sdt \(dqChannel 1\(dq \-m 239.1.1.2:5000 \-r \-e 5
Two stations muxed into one MPTS, RTP-wrapped output, reconnect on input
error after 5 seconds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
Non-zero on argument errors or I/O/network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipimetrics (1),
.BR dipirist (1)
.PP
